fn duplicate_borrow(ptr: *mut i32) {
    let (r1, r2) = unsafe {
        (&mut *ptr, &mut *ptr) // Wildly unsound! Multiple active &mut!
    };
    *r1 = 10;
    *r2 = 20; // Undefined Behavior!
}
```

counterexample:
Utilizing a single exclusive reference, or shared references `&T` combined with safe interior mutability types (`Cell` or `RefCell`):
```rust
fn safe_interior_mutability(cell: &Cell<i32>) {
    cell.set(10);
    cell.set(20); // Perfectly safe, no raw pointer dereference
}
```

fix:
Ensure only a single exclusive mutable reference is active at any given moment, or transition to safe interior mutability containers (`Cell`, `RefCell`, `Mutex`).
```rust
let r1 = unsafe { &mut *ptr };
*r1 = 10; // Lifetime of r1 ends here
let r2 = unsafe { &mut *ptr };
*r2 = 20;
```
